{"title":"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd66075a26de470fc194e67a65f865ce53a57dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{11}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is expressible as the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let us write down one such sum, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> terms and first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d1929fb18a0aed0bfef89cf6949a3d258cd5e17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{11} = (n + 1) + (n + 2) + \\ldots + (n + m) = \\frac{1}{2} m(2n + m + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"466\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54ca5737c8d18c33c77ad8f6190cb6df2714c789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(2n + m + 1) = 2 \\cdot 3^{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisor\" title=\"Divisor\">divisor</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf32f948b07bc396b9e07138c0f0c2471f5465be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{11}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  However, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c98e93d5de890677b11c035ea5515b0369ca04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 &lt; m(m + 1) \\leq 2\\cdot 3^{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/70054f478d051c845dfc1126be376074b7e97c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; \\sqrt{2\\cdot 3^{11}} &lt; 3^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, we are looking for large factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf32f948b07bc396b9e07138c0f0c2471f5465be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{11}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> which are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d440ada8a3f3b7ea6f5beb66cb1834ededc2399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^6$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.  The largest such factor is clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e238e906dbf2072e4af85043b5279f3d7048c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^5 = 486$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />; for this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> we do indeed have the valid <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Expression\" title=\"Expression\">expression</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb10d26f3f1bc9d53801ca90ec0645215f98ae69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{11} = 122 + 123 + \\ldots + 607$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"217\" height=\"16\" />, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/83917f74189e241283af311fc3c293bb9c5a0751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\boxed{486}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the middle term, the sum equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509a0d29031b8cf887718fa94045f61c7a97942e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kn$\" width=\"20\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is even, then we have the sum equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fcdcee7e74cd3f7063826a08e666a27b7e65ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kn+k/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, which will be even. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd66075a26de470fc194e67a65f865ce53a57dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{11}$\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is odd, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd. \n</p><p>Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/f/83fd401497bc8f19f27e5993a1a5e0564116e57a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$nk=3^{11} \\implies n=3^{11}/k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" />. Also, note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da42a5c1fa3f494d2412406a033b2daf677d4e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-(k+1)/2=0 \\implies n=(k+1)/2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"301\" height=\"18\" /> Subsituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce43416fc0e2ba2006d4e4f4cc2fbc177a76c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3^{11}/k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab7dd29afe845aec171087cb262a5770f6fbb2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2+k=2*3^{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />. Proceed as in solution 1.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Proceed as in Solution 1 until it is noted that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf32f948b07bc396b9e07138c0f0c2471f5465be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{11}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. The divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf32f948b07bc396b9e07138c0f0c2471f5465be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{11}$\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5ea38b5900bef0908ce6532f9f1ef4739cfd894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{1} , 2\\cdot 3^{1} , 3^{2} , 2\\cdot 3^{2} , \\ldots , 2\\cdot 3^{10} , 3^{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"254\" height=\"20\" />. Note that the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a5bea241ac747575eec63a8615018474a332b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m(2n + m + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" /> are of opposite parity (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015baf043bd98d7dd0ccef6c53eb9007ecd58151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n + m + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> is even and vice versa). Thus, one of the two factors will be a power of three, and the other will be twice a power of three. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/5/015baf043bd98d7dd0ccef6c53eb9007ecd58151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n + m + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> will represent the greater factor while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> will represent the lesser factor. Given this information, we need to find the factor pair that maximizes the lesser of the two factors, as this will maximize the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. The factor pair which maximizes the lesser factor is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0ea4e70edb36d415dda0775fdc05c91548a1d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3362a845e3303f95706aff47eafb20c047790d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{6}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d0ea4e70edb36d415dda0775fdc05c91548a1d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 3^{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddba87cf3360ca19b1b91c55b94911c18d35929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{486}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME\" title=\"1987 AIME\">1987 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017015356\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 305/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1770/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 92/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7817/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.622      1 -total\n 67.94%   11.973      1 Template:AIME_box\n 30.80%    5.427      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2822:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017015356 and revision id 244615. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}